/-!
# Whole-carrier negative-one control of nonlinear differences

The mixed finite Young estimate is transported through the canonical
frequency cubes to the genuine infinite nonlinear rows.  The result is an
actual weighted `ℓ²(ℤ³; ℂ³)` difference tangent with a cutoff-free bound:

```text
‖N(left) - N(right)‖_{H⁻¹}²
  ≤ 4 * ((M(left)² + M(right)²) * mass(left - right)
      + M(left - right)² * (mass(left) + mass(right))).
```

All three velocity majorants are the actual whole-lattice `tsum`s.
Summability of the difference density and membership in the weighted
carrier are conclusions.  The theorem does not sum a fixed-output norm
bound and does not introduce a terminal shell or frequency cutoff.
-/

